bhaiṣaja,
(1) m. (not recorded in this sense), physician: vaidya- ˚jādayaḥ sulabhāḥ Av 〔ii.167.8〕 (prose);
(2) nt. (= Skt. Lex. id., AMg. bhesaja; Skt. ˚jya), medicine, curing drug; only noted in vss and in positions where ˚jya would be metr. impossible; perh. m.c.?: LV 〔4.3〕 (sa vaidyarājo 'mṛtabhaiṣajapradaḥ); RP 〔22.15〕; 〔23.5〕; 〔26.9〕.
